## Upstream Attribution

GOLI-CLI is an original TypeScript codebase. The architecture and design
documents are derived from the GOLI-CLI Enterprise AI Coding Agent Roadmap
by the same authors. The roadmap is included verbatim under
`docs/source-roadmap/` for reference and traceability.

## Model Backend

GOLI-CLI is designed to operate with **GLM-5.2** (MIT-licensed, open weights)
as its sole default backend. The default client speaks the OpenAI-compatible
Chat Completions API, allowing it to point at:

- A self-hosted vLLM endpoint serving GLM-5.2 FP8 weights (production posture)
- Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (prototype posture)

GOLI-CLI does **not** ship with, depend on, or default to closed-weight vendor
SDKs (Anthropic, OpenAI). Multi-model routing in Module 7 is open-weight-only
by policy; closed-weight providers are hard-blocked in the routing config
(see `docs/decisions/0007-open-weight-only-routing.md`).

## Third-Party Dependencies

A complete Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) is generated on every CI run via
[Syft](https://github.com/anchore/syft). The SBOM is published as a build
artifact and is also committed to `sbom/spdx.json` on tagged releases. The
project's policy is **zero GPL/AGPL dependencies** — see
`docs/decisions/0006-sbom-gate.md` for the rationale and enforcement mechanism.

